      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the Revolutionary War, the Friends Meeting House in Lionville was converted into a hospital for Continental Army soldiers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lionville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Uwchlan Township Historical Commission began in 1975 to champion historic preservation during the National Bicentennial celebration.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uwchlan.com/170/Historical-Commission",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Monthly meetings of the Historical Commission convene at the John Cadwalader House every second Thursday at 7 p.m.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uwchlan.com/170/Historical-Commission",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Inside the Cadwalader House sits the Frances Matthews Library, where township historical documents are carefully archived.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
